# Summary list

Present labelled values when each label has one or more associated answers.

These are civica reference implementations for component authors. They do not replace native Home Assistant behaviour or demonstrate a connection to a live home.

## When to use it

Use it for device details or a review of settings before saving. A summary card can separate several instances of the same thing, each with a unique title.

## When not to use it

Do not use a description list for rows that need comparison across shared columns, a navigation menu or a sequence of tasks. Choose a table, list or task list for those structures.

## Home Assistant adaptation

A device summary should distinguish a friendly name, room and connection state. A settings summary can offer a change link without making the whole row a button. Returning from a change must preserve the existing answer and the path back to the review.

## Accessibility and behaviour

Use dl, dt and dd semantics. Add hidden context to repeated “Change” links, or use a complete visible link label. Keep action targets independent and ensure long values wrap on small screens.

